%% Lifecycle of a protected Contoso file share - the backup item states and the two kinds of recovery point they produce
%% Source: codex/blueprint-azure-files-backup-protection.md, docs/RULES.md (BKP-01, BKP-02, BKP-15); Microsoft Learn "Secure by default with soft delete", "About Azure Files backup" lease section, "Immutable vault" (read 2026-09-03)
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  state "Backup item - one Azure file share in the vault catalog" as ITEM {
    direction TB
    state "Discovered - share listed after the storage account is registered, not protected - assessor BKP-01" as DISC
    state "Protected - policy AFS-Active-4h-30d-Vault-90d - lastBackupStatus Healthy" as PROT
    state "Protected but unhealthy - jobs failing - assessor BKP-02 and BKP-03" as UNH
    state "Stop protection with retain data - no new points, existing ones age out on the policy" as RETAIN
    state "Soft deleted - isScheduledForDeferredDelete true - assessor BKP-15" as SOFT
    state "Permanently deleted - nothing left in Azure Backup" as PURGE

    [*] --> DISC
    DISC --> PROT : Enable-AzRecoveryServicesBackupProtection
    PROT --> UNH : trusted services bypass removed, or allowSharedKeyAccess set to false
    UNH --> PROT : restore bypass AzureServices and key access, then run an on-demand backup
    PROT --> RETAIN : stop backup and retain data - protected by MUA
    PROT --> SOFT : delete backup data - protected by MUA
    RETAIN --> SOFT : delete backup data
    SOFT --> RETAIN : undelete inside the window - the item returns as stop-protection-with-retain-data
    RETAIN --> PROT : resume backup with a policy
    SOFT --> PURGE : soft-delete retention elapses - 14 days by default, configurable 14 to 180
  }

  state "Recovery point - what one backup job leaves behind" as RPOINT {
    direction TB
    state "Snapshot taken through the Files API in the SOURCE storage account" as SNAP
    state "Leased by Azure Backup - infinite lease, so deleting the share is no longer one click" as LEASE
    state "Vault-standard point - changed blocks copied into the vault, offsite" as VAULTRP
    state "Immutable until expiry - vault immutability Enabled or Enabled and locked" as IMMUT
    state "Replicated to the paired region - reachable only by cross-region restore" as PAIRED
    state "Expired and pruned by the policy" as EXP

    [*] --> SNAP
    SNAP --> LEASE : Backup takes the lease at creation, and re-leases before a restore
    LEASE --> VAULTRP : only the LAST scheduled snapshot of the day transfers to the vault
    VAULTRP --> IMMUT : retention can be raised, never shortened, while immutability is on
    IMMUT --> PAIRED : GRS vault with cross-region restore - up to 48 h to appear after enabling
    LEASE --> EXP : snapshot retention 30 days - hard cap of 200 recovery points per share
    IMMUT --> EXP : vault retention from Contoso records schedule - daily 90, monthly 12, yearly 7
  }

  note right of RPOINT
    The asymmetry that decides the design.
    Vault soft delete and vault immutability protect the vault-standard
    points only. Microsoft classes the snapshot tier as an operational
    backup, and states that soft delete and immutability do not apply to
    operational backups of Azure Files. The snapshot chain therefore
    shares the blast radius of the data it protects.
  end note
